# Naming Conventions

## Files and Folders

- Use **kebab-case** for all files and folders
- Examples: `event-list/`, `create-event/`, `user-profile.tsx`

## FSD Segment Files

- Format: `name.type.extension`
- Examples: `user.api.ts`, `user.routes.ts`, `calendar-event.queries.ts`

## File Type Examples

- API: `user.api.ts`, `task.routes.ts`
- Models: `user.types.ts`, `task.schemas.ts`, `journal-entry.queries.ts`
- UI: `event-card.tsx`, `task-item.module.css`

## Component Naming

- Use PascalCase for React components
- Use descriptive names with auxiliary verbs (isLoading, hasError)
- Event handlers should have "handle" prefix: `handleClick`, `handleKeyDown`

## Variable and Function Naming

- Use descriptive names with auxiliary verbs (isLoading, hasError)
- Use functions declarations: `function Component() {}`
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories and files

## CSS Classes

- Use CSS Modules
- Use kebab-case for class names
- Examples: `.container`, `.title`, `.description`

## TypeScript Types and Interfaces

- Use PascalCase for types and interfaces
- Use descriptive names: `Event`, `TaskStatus`, `UserProfile`
- Use suffix for specific types: `EventFormData`, `ApiResponse<T>`

## Constants

- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- Examples: `API_BASE_URL`, `DEFAULT_THEME`, `MAX_TITLE_LENGTH`

## Enum-like Objects

- Use PascalCase for keys
- Use descriptive names: `TaskPriority`, `EventType`
- Prefer const objects over enums
